selIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/1761246301","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1321#issuecomment-1761246301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1321","id":1761246301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX47u85o-nxd","user":{"login":"JankesJanco","id":11212456,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjEyNDU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11212456?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco","html_url":"https://github.com/JankesJanco","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-10-13T09:57:38Z","updated_at":"2023-10-13T09:57:38Z","body":"I ran into a similar issue with this index definition (I think it is not an expression-based index):\r\n\r\n```python\r\nIndex(\"ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first\", latest_sale_date.asc().nullsfirst())\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe index was already created in the database, however after migrating to sqlalchemy2, alembic started to generate drop and create commands for this index. The generated commands are below. Note the difference in the `sa.text()` - in `upgrade()` there is \"latest_sale_date **ASC** NULLS FIRST\" and in `downgrade()` there is just \"latest_sale_date NULLS FIRST\" without \"ASC\"\r\n```python\r\ndef upgrade():\r\n    # ### commands auto generated by Alembic - please adjust! ###\r\n    op.drop_index('ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first', table_name='meme_asset')\r\n    op.create_index('ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first', 'meme_asset', [sa.text('latest_sale_date ASC NULLS FIRST')], unique=False)\r\n    # ### end Alembic commands ###\r\n\r\n\r\ndef downgrade():\r\n    # ### commands auto generated by Alembic - please adjust! ###\r\n    op.drop_index('ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first', table_name='meme_asset')\r\n    op.create_index('ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first', 'meme_asset', [sa.text('latest_sale_date NULLS FIRST')], unique=False)\r\n    # ### end Alembic commands ###\r\n```\r\nWhen I change the index definition in a way that the index is still the same (see below), the drop and create index commands are not being generated anymore (the difference from the first definition is that here we are not using `asc()` which is default)\r\n```python\r\nIndex(\"ix__meme_asset__latest_sale_date__nulls_first\", latest_sale_date.nullsfirst())\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/1761246301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"JankesJanco","id":11212456,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjEyNDU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11212456?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco","html_url":"https://github.com/JankesJanco","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JankesJanco/following{/other_user}"